{"phase": "end", "index": "1", "session": "01a1ac0d-d7fa-7212-ab22-261fd6c30236", "status": 0, "stdout": "In Muster: to wait for a message or a person, just end your turn. Only when you end a turn to wait on work you started (a build, a background job, a sub-agent), first run \"$MUSTER_DAEMON\" report --waiting \"<what>\". Nothing wakes you when a job you started in the background ends, so for one add --until-exits <its pid> (the $! after starting it with &): Muster then messages you when it exits. A wait without it ends after 10 minutes.\n", "stderr": "", "at": "2026-11-05T14:26:01.988581+00:00"}
